{title: Rescue the Perishing}
{artist: Fanny Crosby & William Doane}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[Bb]Rescue the perishing, [Eb]care for the [Bb]dying,
snatch them in pity from [C]sin and the [F]grave;
[Bb]weep o'er the erring one, [Eb]lift up the [Bb]fallen,
tell them of Jesus, the [F]mighty to [Bb]save.

Chorus
[Bb]Rescue the [F]perishing, [Eb]care for the [Bb]dying —
[Bb]Jesus is [Eb]merciful, [Bb]Jesus will [F]save.

Verse 2
[Bb]Though they are slighting [Eb]Him, still He is [Bb]waiting,
Waiting the penitent child to receive; Plead [C]with them earnestly, plead [F]with
[Bb]them gently; He will forgive they should [Eb]only believe. Rescue the [Bb]perishing,
care for the dying, Jesus is [F]merciful, Jesus will [Bb]save.

Verse 3
[Bb]Down in the human [Eb]heart, crushed by the tempter, [Bb]Feelings
lie buried that grace can restore; Touched [C]by a loving heart, [F]wakened
[Bb]by kindness, Chords that were broken will [Eb]vibrate once more. Rescue [Bb]the
perishing, care for the dying, Jesus is [F]merciful, Jesus will [Bb]save.

Verse 4
[Bb]Rescue the perishing, duty [Eb]demands it; Strength for [Bb]thy
labor the Lord will provide; Back to [C]the narrow way patiently [F]win
[Bb]them; Tell the poor wand'rer a Savior [Eb]has died. Rescue the [Bb]perishing,
care for the dying, Jesus is [F]merciful, Jesus will [Bb]save.
